From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Majer <17414256+tpmajer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:54:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: hand over to a session on a VT of its own

A session was started on the greeter's VT once the greeter had
exited, in text mode: the VT showed between two compositors, and
giving the display back to the console takes the kernel half a second
here.

With `terminal.handover` the session is started at once on the next
free VT, in graphics mode, while the greeter is still up. The VT is
switched to once the PAM session is open, so that logind knows of the
session on it and starts no getty, and so that little can fail with
the greeter out of sight; if the start fails all the same, the
greeter's VT is switched back to. The greeter is terminated a few
seconds later: what it last showed stays on the display until the
session's compositor takes it, and would go with the greeter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
